,NULL,'native, YK, MK, KW, FK, LB, MB-NF, ne cont. USA (mtns.,ME, NH); also in Greenland, Iceland, Eurasia. Current authors prefer the syn., based on Poa pratensis var. alpigena Fr.','alpigena',''),(3981,'(Fr.) Schol.','','','',NULL,'Poa',NULL,NULL,'native, FK, Greenland. Also = Poa pratensis L. ssp. alpigena (Fr.) Hiitonen.','alpigena','var. colpodea'),(3982,'L.','','','',NULL,'Poa',NULL,NULL,'native, rocky shores, outcrops, crevices, n AK, MK, KW, FK, Ungava-LB, BC-PQ, NS, NF, nw-nc cont. USA; also in Greenland, Iceland, Eurasia.','alpina',''),(3983,'Merr.','','big bluegrass','',NULL,'Poa',NULL,NULL,'native, meadows, moist open ground, dry rocky slopes, se AK, YK, BC-s SK, w cont. USA.','ampla',''),(3984,'L.','','annual bluegrass, low speargrass','gazon, pâturin annuel',NULL,'Poa',NULL,NULL,'introduced, native to Eurasia; natzd., Aleutian Is., AK, YK, BC-NF, e cont. USA; also in St. Pierre & Miq. (var. reptans Hausskn.), Greenland.','annua',''),(3985,'R. Br.','','','',NULL,'Poa',NULL,NULL,'native, tundra, shores of ponds and streams, Aleutian Is., AK, YK, MK, KW, FK, Ungava-LB, BC, AB, n MB-PQ, s LB, NF, w cont. USA (mtns.); also in Greenland, Iceland, Eurasia.','arctica',''),(3986,'R. Br.','','','',NULL,'Poa',NULL,NULL,'native, tundra, shores of ponds and streams, Aleutian Is., AK, YK, MK, KW, FK, Ungava-LB, BC, AB, n MB-PQ, s LB, NF, w cont. USA (mtns.); also in Greenland, Iceland, Eurasia.','arctica','var. arctica f. arctica'),(3988,'(Nannf.) B. Boivin','','','',NULL,'Poa',NULL,NULL,'native, FK, n MB, n PQ; also in Greenland. Tzvelev (1976) considers this plant a hybrid sp. and refers it to Poa tolmatchewii Roshev. or possibly to Poa filipes Lange, descr. from Greenland.','arctica','var. caespitans'),(3991,'Vasey','','','',NULL,'Poa',NULL,NULL,'native, prairies, plains, alkaline flats, s BC-MB, w cont. USA.','arida',''),(3992,'L.','','bulbous bluegrass','',NULL,'Poa',NULL,NULL,'introduced, native to Eurasia; s BC, e, w (coastal) cont. USA.','bulbosa',''),(3993,