 BC, s AB, nw cont. USA.','caeruleum','subsp. villosum'),(4038,'Hook.','','','',NULL,'Polemonium',NULL,NULL,'native, dry to moist rocky areas, alpine, AK, YK, MK, BC, sw AB, w cont. USA (Rocky Mtns.).','pulcherrimum',''),(4039,'L.','','','',NULL,'Polemonium',NULL,NULL,'Temperate Eurasia, North America, Chile.','',''),(4040,'Willd.','','bird-on-the-wing, flowering wintergreen, fringed polygala','polygala paucifolié',NULL,'Polygala',NULL,NULL,'native, moist woodlands, SK-NB, nec cont. USA.','paucifolia',''),(4041,'L.','','Senega snakeroot','sénéca',NULL,'Polygala',NULL,NULL,'native, woods, praireis, s AB-w NB, nc-ec cont. USA.','senega',''),(4042,'(Walter) Elliott','','two-flowered Solomon\'s-seal','sceau-de-Salomon … deux fleurs',NULL,'Polygonatum',NULL,NULL,'native, moist woods, thickets, se SK-sw PQ, c cont. USA; also in Mexico.','biflorum',''),(4043,'(Willd.) Pursh','','downy Solomon\'s seal','sceau-de-Salomon pubescent',NULL,'Polygonatum',NULL,NULL,'native, rich rocky woods, thickets, ON-NS, e cont. USA.','pubescens',''),(4045,'Blake','','erect knotweed','renouée dressée',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'native, widespread, dry open ground, roadsides, AK, YK, MK, BC-NS, NF, nc-e cont. USA. Often confused with Polygonum erectum L. which is rare, and differs in many features except an erect habit and broad leaves.','achoreum',''),(4046,'L.','','amphibious bistort, water smartweed','renouée amphibie',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'native, shallow water, shores, swamps, ditches, wet meadows, AK, YK, MK, BC-NF, n cont. USA; also in Iceland, Eurasia.','amphibium',''),(4050,'(Coleman) Fern.','','amphibious bistort, water smartweed.','renouée amphibie',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'native, shallow water, swamps, wet meadows, AK, YK, MK, BC-NF, n cont. USA. Also = Polygonum amphibium L. ssp. laevimarginatum Hultén.','amphibium','var. stipulaceum'),(4052,'(Eat.) Fern.','','floating amphibious bistort, water smartweed','renouée amphibie',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'native, shallow water, swamps, wet meadows, AK, YK, MK, BC-NF, n cont. USA. Type of the form described from PQ. Almost fully aquatic form with long-petioled leaves.','amphibium','var. stipulaceum f. fluitans'),(4054,'Jord. ex Boreau','','','',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'introduced, native to Eurasia; AK, YK, MK, AB-NF, ne cont. USA. Many reports of the hexaploid Polygonum aviculare L. may refer to this weedy tetraploid sp. found in ruderal habitats.','arenastrum',''),(4057,'L.','','common knotweed, prostrate knotweed','renouée des oiseaux',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'introduced, native to Eurasia, AK, YK, BC-NF, n cont. USA. Many Can. reports have been referred to Polygonum arenastrum Jord. ex Boreau, a tetraploid plant, but the sp. is hexaploid. McNeill (1981), unlike Scoggan, considers it widespread in CD.','aviculare',''),(4058,'L.','','bistort','',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'native, grassy tundra, ledges, AK, YK, MK, NS; also in Eurasia.','bistorta',''),(4059,'(Small) Hultén','','bistort','',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'native, AK, YK, MK n to Arctic coast.','bistorta','subsp. plumosum'),(4061,'Pursh','','bistort, smokeweed','',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'native, streambanks, moist or swampy meadows, alpine slopes, s BC, sw AB, w cont. USA.','bistortoides',''),(4062,'Small','','','',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'native, prairies, roadsides and other disturbed sites, BC-NF, n cont. USA. The Eurasian syn. differs from the sp. in morphological features such as the structure of the achenes. Both belong to the Polygonum aviculaire L. aggregate.','buxiforme',''),(4064,'Michx.','','fringed black bindweed','renouée … noeuds ciliés',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'native, dry thickets, rocky slopes, SK-NF, nc-ne cont. USA.','cilinode',''),(4065,'L.','','black bindweed, wild buckwheat','chevrier, renouée liseron',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'introduced, native to Eurasia; natzd. as weed, AK, s YK, s MK, BC-NF, n cont. USA; also in s Greenland.','convolvulus',''),(4066,'Engelm. & Gray','','climbing false buckwheat','',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'introduced, native to sc cont. USA. Now treated as Polygonum scandens L. var. cristatum (Engelm. & A. Gray) Gleason. Believed to be the Polygonum scandens L. of some Can. reports from s BC & s AB','cristatum',''),(4067,'Siebold & Zucc.','','fleece-flower, Japanese knot-weed','',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'introduced, native to e Asia; cult., garden escape, as in BC, MB-NF, cont. USA.','cuspidatum',''),(4068,'L.','','erect knotweed','renouée dressée',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'native, dry open ground, roadsides, AK, YK, MK, BC-NS, NF, nc-e cont. USA. A rare sp. locally concentrated in CD in c AB and s ON. Many reports and herb. specimens confused with Polygonum achoreum Blake, q.v. (McNeill 1986).','erectum',''),(4069,'B.L. Robins.','','Fowler\'s knotweed','',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'native, sandy, gravelly seashores, coastal saltmarshes, AK, coastal BC-WA; n MB-PQ (Hudson and James Bay), coastal LB, NF, NS, n Maine, PQ (St. Lawrence estuary); also in ?e Asia.  Distinguished by different early and late season fruits.','fowleri',''),(4071,'L.','','common smartweed, water pepper','curage, renouée poivre-d\'eau',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'native, damp soils, ditches, se AK, s BC, MB-NF, w-ec cont. USA; also in Eurasia.','hydropiper',''),(4072,'Michx.','','false water pepper, mild water pepper','renouée faux-poivre-d\'eau',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'native, wet ground, shores, shallow water, s BC, ON-NS, cont. USA; also in Mexico, South America.','hydropiperoides',''),(4073,'L.','','dock-leaved knotweed, pale smartweed, willow-weed','renouée … feuilles de patience, - feuilles d\'oiselle',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'native, swampy thickets, shores, damp clearings, fields, BC-NF, n cont. USA; also in Iceland, Eurasia. Introduced in AK, MK, Greenland.','lapathifolium',''),(4074,'Sibth.','','willow-leaved smartweed, willow-weed','',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'native, swampy thickets, shores, damp clearings, fields, BC-NF, n cont. USA.','lapathifolium','var. salicifolium'),(4075,'Besser','','','',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'native?, widespread weed, disturbed soil, roadsides, gardens, etc., AK, YK, MK, AB-NF, c-e cont. USA. Differs from the tetraploid syn. in having 2 chromosome races and other morphological features. Fern. treated it as the type of P. aviculare L.','neglectum',''),(4077,'L.','','kiss-me-over-the-garden-gate, Prince\'s plume, lady\'s thumb','monte-au-ciel',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'introduced, native to Asia; cult. as ornamental, spreading from cultivation to roadsides, waste areas, ON, PQ.','orientale',''),(4078,'(L.) Sm.','','knotweed, pinkweed','renouée de Pennsylvanie',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'native, shores, thickets, clearings, cult. ground, ON-NS, e cont. USA; introduced into AK, BC.','pensylvanicum',''),(4079,'L.','','heart\'s-ease, lady\'s thumb','fer … cheval, renouée persicaire',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'introduced, native to Eurasia; roadsides, damp clearings, cultivated fields, s AK, BC-NF, e cont. USA; introduced into Greenland.','persicaria',''),(4080,'Meisn. ex Small','','alpine knotweed','',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'native, subalpine or alpine meadows, talus slopes, ridges, AK, YK, MK, ?BC, w cont. USA (mtns.); also in e Siberia.','phytolaccifolium',''),(4082,'Elliott','','water smartweed','renouée ponctuée',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'native, wet areas, swampy ground, s BC, SK-PE., cont. USA; also in tropical America, s Asia.','punctatum',''),(4083,'(Meisn.) Fassett','','water smartweed','renouée ponctuée',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'native, wet areas, swampy ground, s BC, SK-PE, cont. USA; also in Mexico.','punctatum','var. confertiflorum'),(4085,'(Meisn.) Small','','water smartweed','renouée ponctuée',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NULL,'native, wet areas, swampy ground, NS, e-sc cont. USA; also in Mexico. = Polygonum robustus (Small) Fern.','punctatum','var. majus'),(4086,'Elliott','','water smartweed','renouée ponctuée',NULL,'Polygonum',NULL,NU